1
00:00:00,910 --> 00:00:18,310
As we witness the advancement of forces of wickedness further into Palestine to continue to commit acts that are governed by a body that we know is not of the spirit or of the soul, it makes for many of us a feeling of hopelessness.

2
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:35,660
And though I am not a religious person, I do connect with the spirit and I am a believer that we as a unit are the spirit and we can make change.

3
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:42,040
And so I invite you to raise your voices and read with me this prayer posted by the brilliant Orson Shire.

4
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:48,220
Bismillah ar-Rahman ar-Rahim. In the name of Allah, the most gracious, the most merciful.

5
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:54,260
Ya Allah, the sustainer of all worlds, we turn to you in desperate plea for the Palestinian people.

6
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:56,980
Protect them from the bombardment they face.

7
00:00:57,680 --> 00:01:01,600
Shield them from the siege and save them from the hands that aim to harm them.

8
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:07,500
Ya Rahman, mend the broken hearts of those who have lost their homes, family and hope.

9
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:14,300
Strengthen their Iman in times of despair and grant them unwavering saber in their struggles.

10
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:18,380
Raise their ranks among the righteous and the martyrs in the hereafter.

11
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:23,240
Ya Mu'iz, empower them with resilience and fortitude.

12
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:29,400
Grant them the victory that you promised to the oppressed and let them reclaim their rights and their lands.

13
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:33,700
Ya Ar-Rahman ar-Rahman, shower them with your infinite mercy.

14
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:39,760
Comfort the grieving mother, the frightened child, the desperate father and every soul in pain.

15
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:45,280
Let their tears be a testament to their patience and their unwavering faith in you.

16
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:51,320
Ya Jabbar, mend their communities, heal their wounds and fortify their spirits.

17
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:55,240
Bestow upon them the means to rebuild, making them stronger than before.

18
00:01:56,180 --> 00:02:04,520
Ya Allah, hasten the day of their liberation, where peace and justice reign and where they can live in their lands freely and without fear.

19
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:12,080
Grant them justice against their oppressors and let those who inflict harm upon them be humiliated in this world and the next.

20
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:13,220
Amin.

